<%- include('partials/header') %>
<%- include('partials/navbar') %>

<main class="about-page">
    <div class="container py-4 py-lg-5 mt-5">
        <section class="about-hero mb-4">
            <div class="row g-0 align-items-stretch">
                <div class="col-lg-6 d-flex align-items-center">
                    <div class="about-hero-copy">
                        <span class="about-eyebrow"><i class="ri-sparkling-2-line me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> About CareerGuide AI · Your next chapter starts here</span>
                        <h1>Make your next career move <span>with clarity.</span></h1>
                        <p class="about-lead">Big career questions can feel easier when you take them one step at a time. CareerGuide AI brings career exploration, skill planning, resume feedback, and interview practice together to help students move from “Where do I start?” to a next step they can work on.</p>
                        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4">
                            <a href="/auth/register" class="btn btn-primary rounded-pill px-4 py-2">Start exploring <i class="ri-arrow-right-line ms-1" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                            <a href="#career-journey" class="btn btn-outline-primary rounded-pill px-4 py-2">See how it works</a>
                        </div>
                        <p class="about-hero-note mb-0 mt-3">Helpful guidance for your decisions—not promises about a specific outcome.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6">
                    <figure class="about-hero-visual mb-0">
                        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523580494863-6f3031224c94?auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=1400&amp;q=85"
                             alt="Students celebrating together at graduation" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
                        <div class="about-hero-image-shade"></div>
                        <figcaption class="about-photo-caption"><i class="ri-image-line me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Illustrative student photo · <a href="https://unsplash.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Unsplash</a></figcaption>
                        <div class="about-image-note"><i class="ri-compass-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Explore <b>·</b> Learn <b>·</b> Prepare</span></div>
                    </figure>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-mission mb-4">
            <div class="about-mission-mark"><i class="ri-focus-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
            <div>
                <span class="about-section-label">Our mission</span>
                <h2>Make career preparation feel less overwhelming.</h2>
                <p>We bring role exploration, skill-building guidance, resume review, and interview practice into one place. Instead of facing career planning as one huge decision, students can break it into questions they can answer and actions they can take at their own pace. CareerGuide AI is here to make those first steps clearer, while leaving every important choice in the student's hands.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-vision mb-4">
            <div class="about-vision-art" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="about-orbit about-orbit-one"></div>
                <div class="about-orbit about-orbit-two"></div>
                <div class="about-vision-icon"><i class="ri-eye-line"></i></div>
                <span class="about-orbit-label orbit-label-one">Your goals</span>
                <span class="about-orbit-label orbit-label-two">Your pace</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-vision-copy">
                <span class="about-section-label">Our vision</span>
                <h2>Career guidance that meets you where you are.</h2>
                <p>We want useful career guidance to be more accessible, practical, and personal. Whether you are comparing career directions, building skills, or preparing to apply, the platform can help you turn broad ambitions into useful questions and possible next steps. As interests and experience change, your plans can change too.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-journey mb-4" id="career-journey">
            <div class="about-heading-center">
                <span class="about-section-label">A simple path forward</span>
                <h2>One question at a time.<br><span>A clearer next step.</span></h2>
                <p>You don't need a perfect plan before you begin. Start with what's on your mind, then use each step to decide what might help next.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-journey-grid">
                <article class="about-journey-step">
                    <span class="about-journey-index">01</span>
                    <div class="about-journey-icon"><i class="ri-compass-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                    <h3>Explore possible roles</h3>
                    <p>Learn about responsibilities, common skills, and the kind of work different careers involve.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="about-journey-step">
                    <span class="about-journey-index">02</span>
                    <div class="about-journey-icon"><i class="ri-search-eye-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                    <h3>Understand your starting point</h3>
                    <p>Compare your experience with a role's skills and identify areas to build further.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="about-journey-step">
                    <span class="about-journey-index">03</span>
                    <div class="about-journey-icon"><i class="ri-route-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                    <h3>Prepare with a plan</h3>
                    <p>Organize learning into manageable steps that fit your goals and study time.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="about-journey-step">
                    <span class="about-journey-index">04</span>
                    <div class="about-journey-icon"><i class="ri-rocket-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                    <h3>Practise and keep moving</h3>
                    <p>Improve your resume, rehearse interview questions, and track opportunities.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-tools mb-4">
            <div class="about-tools-heading">
                <div>
                    <span class="about-section-label">Your career toolkit</span>
                    <h2>Everything has a next step.</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Practical tools for the questions students often face—from choosing a direction to feeling ready to apply.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row g-3">
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-blue"><i class="ri-robot-2-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>AI Career Guidance</h3>
                        <p>Ask about career choices, skills, resumes, or interview preparation. Use the response to organize your thoughts and find questions worth exploring—not as a substitute for your own research.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Explore with context</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-violet"><i class="ri-file-text-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>Resume ATS Checker</h3>
                        <p>Review a PDF or DOCX resume against a target role and optional job description. Use feedback to spot details to clarify, then make sure every claim reflects your actual experience.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Present your experience</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-green"><i class="ri-bar-chart-box-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>Skill Gap Analyzer</h3>
                        <p>Compare skills you enter with those associated with a target role. Use the result to identify potential learning priorities; it is a guide, not a formal assessment.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Find a learning focus</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-amber"><i class="ri-road-map-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>Career Roadmaps</h3>
                        <p>Build a suggested learning plan around a target role, experience, skills, and study time. Adapt the steps as your interests, schedule, and knowledge change.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Turn goals into steps</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-rose"><i class="ri-question-answer-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>AI Mock Interviews</h3>
                        <p>Practise technical multiple-choice questions, review explanations, and revisit completed attempts to find topics that may need more practice.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Practise with purpose</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
                    <article class="about-tool-card h-100">
                        <div class="about-tool-icon tool-cyan"><i class="ri-briefcase-4-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <h3>Jobs, Internships & Applications</h3>
                        <p>Browse available listings, review the information provided, and record applications you want to track. Confirm current requirements with the original listing.</p>
                        <span class="about-tool-tag">Keep your search organized</span>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-audience mb-4">
            <div class="about-audience-icon"><i class="ri-user-heart-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
            <div>
                <span class="about-section-label">Made for the in-between moments</span>
                <h2>For students figuring out what comes next.</h2>
                <p>Maybe you have a goal but aren't sure how to reach it. Maybe you have skills but don't know how to show them. Or maybe you're still exploring. You don't need to have everything figured out—bring one question, one interest, or one small goal, and start there.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-audience-doodle" aria-hidden="true"><i class="ri-arrow-right-up-line"></i></div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-feature-story mb-4">
            <div class="about-story-image">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1522202176988-66273c2fd55f?auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=1100&amp;q=85"
                     alt="Students collaborating around a table" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
                <span class="about-story-image-label"><i class="ri-lightbulb-flash-line me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Curiosity is a good place to start</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-story-copy">
                <span class="about-section-label">Explore directions</span>
                <h2>Discover careers beyond job titles.</h2>
                <p>A role is more than its name. Learn about responsibilities, common skills, and the work involved, then compare options that catch your interest. You may find new questions to research or skills that connect more than one path.</p>
                <p>Use career information as a starting point for further research and conversations. Requirements can differ between employers, so check what applies to the role and industry you are exploring.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-skills mb-4">
            <div class="about-skills-copy">
                <span class="about-section-label">Know your starting point</span>
                <h2>Turn skill gaps into learning priorities.</h2>
                <p>It's hard to plan what to learn when the goal feels far away. Compare the skills you enter with those connected to a target role to notice possible strengths and areas to practise. The result can help you choose one useful focus instead of trying to learn everything at once.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">This comparison is guidance based on the information provided—not a pass/fail grade or a complete measure of your ability.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-skills-visual" aria-label="A simple illustration of comparing skills and choosing a learning focus">
                <div class="about-skill-column">
                    <span class="about-skill-overline">Your starting point</span>
                    <span class="about-skill-pill"><i class="ri-check-line"></i> Skills you have</span>
                    <span class="about-skill-pill"><i class="ri-check-line"></i> Projects & experience</span>
                </div>
                <div class="about-skill-connector"><i class="ri-arrow-right-line"></i></div>
                <div class="about-skill-column skill-focus">
                    <span class="about-skill-overline">A next focus</span>
                    <span class="about-skill-pill"><i class="ri-focus-3-line"></i> Practise a skill</span>
                    <span class="about-skill-pill"><i class="ri-book-open-line"></i> Learn step by step</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-roadmap mb-4">
            <div class="about-roadmap-copy">
                <span class="about-section-label">Make a learning plan</span>
                <h2>Big goals feel better in smaller steps.</h2>
                <p>Career Roadmaps help organize possible learning steps around a target role, your current skills, experience, and study time. Use a roadmap to pick a manageable topic, practise what you learn, and build toward your wider goal without treating the plan as fixed.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">As you gain experience or discover new interests, adjust the plan. Your route can change as you do.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-roadmap-visual" aria-label="Illustrative learning roadmap">
                <div class="about-roadmap-line"></div>
                <div class="about-roadmap-stop"><span>01</span><div><strong>Choose a direction</strong><small>Start with a role or question</small></div></div>
                <div class="about-roadmap-stop"><span>02</span><div><strong>Pick one learning focus</strong><small>Make the next step manageable</small></div></div>
                <div class="about-roadmap-stop"><span>03</span><div><strong>Practise and review</strong><small>Adapt as you make progress</small></div></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-preparation mb-4">
            <div class="about-heading-center">
                <span class="about-section-label">Get application-ready</span>
                <h2>Prepare to show what you can do.</h2>
                <p>Preparation is about communicating your real strengths clearly and giving yourself space to practise.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row g-3">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <article class="about-prep-card resume-prep h-100">
                        <div class="about-prep-top"><span class="about-prep-icon"><i class="ri-file-edit-line"></i></span><span class="about-prep-tag">Your story on paper</span></div>
                        <h3>Make your resume easier to understand.</h3>
                        <p>The Resume ATS Checker reviews your PDF or DOCX against a target role and optional job description. Its feedback can help you notice experience to clarify or wording to review. Keep your final resume truthful, specific, and representative of your work.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <article class="about-prep-card interview-prep h-100">
                        <div class="about-prep-top"><span class="about-prep-icon"><i class="ri-chat-voice-line"></i></span><span class="about-prep-tag">Practice builds comfort</span></div>
                        <h3>Rehearse, reflect, and try again.</h3>
                        <p>Practise technical questions, review explanations, and revisit completed mock interviews to see what to study next. Practice can build familiarity, but no question bank can promise what a real interview will ask or how it will go.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-opportunities mb-4">
            <div class="about-opportunities-art"><i class="ri-briefcase-4-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><i class="ri-map-pin-2-line" aria-hidden="true"></i> Your next opportunity</span></div>
            <div class="about-opportunities-copy">
                <span class="about-section-label">Explore opportunities</span>
                <h2>Keep your search moving—and organized.</h2>
                <p>Browse available job and internship listings, review the details provided, and record applications you want to follow. Keeping your search organized can make it easier to remember where you applied and what you may want to do next.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">Listings and requirements can change, so always confirm deadlines, eligibility, and application instructions with the original employer or listing.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-principles mb-4">
            <div class="about-principles-heading">
                <span class="about-section-label">A thoughtful way to use AI</span>
                <h2>A guide beside you.<br><span>Your choices stay yours.</span></h2>
            </div>
            <div class="about-principles-list">
                <div><i class="ri-user-smile-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><p><strong>Your context matters.</strong> Interests, education, experience, and circumstances all shape what advice is useful.</p></div>
                <div><i class="ri-seedling-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><p><strong>Progress can be gradual.</strong> Focus on a skill, a resume improvement, or one practice session at a time.</p></div>
                <div><i class="ri-shield-check-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><p><strong>Verify important details.</strong> AI suggestions can be incomplete; check reliable sources and adapt them to your situation.</p></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-cta">
            <div class="about-cta-content">
                <span class="about-section-label">Your next step</span>
                <h2>Start with one question.<br>See where it takes you.</h2>
                <p>Explore your options, make a plan, or practise for what's ahead. Create an account to start using the career tools, or log in to continue your journey.</p>
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                    <a href="/auth/register" class="btn btn-light rounded-pill px-4 py-2 fw-semibold">Create an account <i class="ri-arrow-right-line ms-1" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                    <a href="/auth/login" class="btn btn-outline-light rounded-pill px-4 py-2">Log in</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="about-cta-decoration" aria-hidden="true"><i class="ri-send-plane-2-line"></i></div>
        </section>
    </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
